# Declarations for the DPV Locations resource: ISO distinctness.
#
# Generated from the rule that ISO 3166 assigns one code per area, so that
# two areas listed by the extension are two places.  The extension asserts
# none of this; the rule is a declaration, and a verdict resting on it is
# withdrawable by abandoning the rule.
#
# The distinctness is between areas, not between codes.  The extension
# records 27 places under two codes, a country code and a
# subdivision code for the same area, and those pairs are identified rather
# than separated.  Distinctness is asserted between the classes those
# identities induce, and the members below name one class each, by its
# country code where it has one.
#
# Not listed: DK-GL and GB-JSY. DPV Locations lists each of these areas
# under two codes (GL and DK-GL, JE and GB-JSY) with no identity
# statement, so listing both codes would declare one area distinct from
# itself.
#
# DPV identifies BQ with each of NL-BQ1, NL-BQ2 and NL-BQ3, and SJ with
# NO-21 and NO-22, so each group falls into one identity class and the ISO
# rule cannot separate Bonaire, Saba and Sint Eustatius from one another,
# or Svalbard from Jan Mayen. This is DPV's published data, to be reported
# upstream.
#
# Greenland (DK-GL) and Jersey (GB-JSY) are left out for the reason stated
# above.
#
# Classes: 4977
# Pairs  : 12382776
# Source : https://w3id.org/dpv/2.3/loc

@prefix loc:     <https://w3id.org/dpv/loc#> .
@prefix bind:    <https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/binding#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/dpv-loc/iso> a bind:Declarations ;
    dcterms:title "Pairwise distinctness of ISO 3166 areas"@en ;
    bind:appliesTo <https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/dpv-loc-geo>,
                 <https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/dpv-loc-juris> ;
    bind:generatedBy bind:PairwiseDistinctness ;
    bind:origin bind:practiceRule ;
    rdfs:comment "The origin rests on the ISO 3166 rule that a code names one area. The part of DPV Locations used here has 4,979 identity classes and the set lists 4,977 of them; the scope names the 2 left out and why."@en ;
    bind:scopeCondition "Distinctness holds between equivalence classes under the extension's identity statements, not between codes; codes the extension identifies name one area. Not listed: DK-GL and GB-JSY. DPV Locations lists each of these areas under two codes (GL and DK-GL, JE and GB-JSY) with no identity statement, so listing both codes would declare one area distinct from itself."@en ;
    bind:pairCount 12382776 ;
